## Context

Child of 0029 (tracker). The author's rulings of 2026-09-06 (DECISIONS.md, two
entries; conception/0029-golden-fixture-structure-review.md Parts D and E) fix
the Menagerie's shape: two sampled strata (a representative core following the
census marginals of ticket 0711, defect rates included, and an adversarial
reserve enumerated from 0029's coverage ledger and the pathology ledger), scale
surrogates as generators outside the export; topics of the author's own library
(economics, uncertainty, energy, environment, development, STS, HSS), no
animals; documents in all nine R7 languages, multilingual documents, legacy
encodings of the 1990s as authentic archive-issued files; format mix PDF 56,9 %
/ HTML 33,0 % / other 9,2 %; the five-part admission test; Wikipedia ordinary,
interlanguage links recorded as same-subject; Gallica dropped; HAL and FAOLEX
narrow exceptions. Ticket 0632's export (PR #381) recorded eight known defects
and a limits-ignored reindex; this child repairs them and re-exports.

## Recipe schema, extended (the contract every sourcing lane writes to)

Parent record (the `attachments` shape of `fetch_recipe.py`): the existing
required fields plus
- `topic`: one of economics, uncertainty, energy, environment, development,
  sts, hss;
- `stratum`: core or reserve;
- `language_field`: the exact string written to Zotero's `language` field
  ("" or a malformed spelling on purpose for about half the core, per the
  census: 78 spellings, half empty); the recipe's `language` stays the
  declared language of the work and defines nothing for the lane;
- `mechanisms`: list of mechanism ids a reserve member carries (empty for core);
- `retained_reason`: required on any off-topic record kept from the old recipe;
- `citation`: `{doi, isbn, url}` (any subset), written to the Zotero fields
  the item type has, so the citation chain of ruling 7 has an identifier;
- `notes`: optional list of `{id, html}` child notes (managed marker
  `zoteus-golden-note:<id>`);
- `work_relations` gains the type `same-subject` (Wikipedia interlanguage
  links, never `translation`).

Attachment record: the existing required fields plus
- `charset`: required for every text format (`utf-8`, or the authentic legacy
  charset: `windows-1258`, `koi8-r`, `windows-1251`, `gb2312`, `big5`,
  `iso-8859-1`, `windows-1256`, ...), written explicitly on the Zotero item;
- `bytes_format` widened: pdf, djvu, wikitext, txt, html, epub, docx, xlsx,
  odt, rtf, md, jpg, png, zip, tgz (unindexable formats are failure controls);
- `content_type_declared`: optional, for the lying-MIME failure control only;
- `encoding_note`: optional prose on a legacy encoding.

Archives are data: `bench/fixtures/archives.json` carries each admitted
archive's hosts, identifier form, version rule and its admission probe under
the five-part test (date, URL fetched, status, licence, age). A new archive is
admitted by recording a real probe, not by editing a frozenset.

## Relevant files
- `bench/fixtures/recipe.json`, `recipe-pinned.json`, `select_hashed.py`
- `bench/fixtures/fetch_recipe.py` (validator + fetch), `archives.json` (new)
- `bench/fixtures/golden_fixture.py` (inject/export), `make_index_fixture.mjs`
- `bench/zotero-fulltext-plugin/bootstrap.js` (reindex `complete` flag)
- `bench/fixtures/README.md`, `bench/fixtures/export/`
- `tests/test_fixture_recipe.py`, `tests/test_golden_fixture_harness.py`

## Actions
1. Plugin: `POST reindex` takes `complete` (default false = stock limits);
   `status` reports the plugin version and the mode of the last reindex.
2. Harness: explicit charset on every text attachment; `--reindex-mode
   stock|uncapped` (stock default) recorded in the manifest as observed, both
   preferences read from the client; per-attachment counters; child notes;
   `language_field`, `citation`, `topic`, `stratum`, `mechanisms` written and
   exported; a retire step that moves a parent out of the collection (no
   deletion); a body-text check on text attachments (no transclusion skeleton).
3. Recipe: retire off-topic records that carry no unique mechanism, keep the
   rest with `retained_reason`; source the core to the census marginals and
   the reserve to the ledgers; re-pin the two Wikisource skeletons to full
   text; hash every new attachment into `~/data/golden-fixture-cache`.
4. Inject into group 6659303 / collection 3AY48MA5 from padme over ssh as
   0632's 2026-09-06 run did; re-export; replay through
   `make_index_fixture.mjs --replay-export`; commit `export/`.

## Verification
